WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.500
Goooood morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.640
It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer
real questions from real nerdfighters.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.979
It's actually the previous Friday, but I'm
going on vacation, so if anything important

00:00:07.979 --> 00:00:10.910
has happened in the intervening four days
that I'm not talking about it, it's because

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.910
I don't know!

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:12.910
Let's get to the questions.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:13.910
Q: BEARD?!

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:14.910
A: Yeah, I'm kinda growing a beard.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:15.910
I dunno, Sarah wants me to.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:16.910
What do you think?

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.539
Q: Why do none of the main characters in your
books have siblings?

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:22.170
A: It's just my little way of letting Hank
know that in my narrative imagination, he

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.170
does not exist.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.749
Q: Do you still have your Holden Caulfield
hat?

00:00:24.749 --> 00:00:26.429
A: You mean my people-hunting hat?

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:27.429
Yes.

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:28.429
Q: Apples or oranges?

00:00:28.429 --> 00:00:30.480
A: I don't know, I find it difficult to compare
them.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.129
Q: In your book Looking for Alaska, was Alaska's
'blank' a 'blank' or a 'blank?'

00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:35.129
A: I don't know.

00:00:35.129 --> 00:00:37.110
Also, that's not really the question for me.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.260
The question is whether we can live hopeful
and thoughtful lives in spite of ambiguity,

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.329
in spite of the fact that important questions
go unanswered.

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:46.440
Q: Hey when's the Paper Towns movie come out?

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.079
A:There's an important question I will not
leave unanswered, June fifth!

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:52.539
I just watched like ten minutes of the movie
that Jake Schreier showed me when I was in

00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:54.190
Los Angeles and I'm so excited, Hank!

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.039
Q: Do you have any productivity tips?

00:00:56.039 --> 00:00:57.039
A: Yeah.

00:00:57.039 --> 00:00:58.969
So first, procrastinate for a while.

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:00.249
Longer... longer...

00:01:00.249 --> 00:01:05.549
wait until you feel, like, that sour panic-adrenaline
in the back of your throat and then GO GO

00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:06.549
GO GO GO GO GO!

00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:09.130
That's a terrible productivity tip, but it's
the only one I have.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.780
Q: How many licks does it take to get to the
center of a Tootsie pop?

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.640
A: Between 115 and 500 and yes, there are
studies about this.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.640
Links in the dooblydoo.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:16.670
Q: Favorite Art Assignment video?

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:19.020
A: Pretty fond of Christoph Niemann's emotional
furniture.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.550
I also really enjoyed the highlights video
where I got to make some prints with Sarah.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:23.550
Links in the dooblydoo.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.550
Q: Favorite song by Taylor Swift?

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.820
A: Probably Blank Space, or as Henry calls
it, "Boys Love Torture!"

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.680
Q: Hey, are you writing a new book?

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.680
A: Yeah, I'm..

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:31.680
I'm trying to!

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:32.680
Q: But are you writing, really?

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.680
Are you writing it?

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.680
A: Yes!

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:35.680
Q: But ARE YOU WRITING A NEW BOOK?!

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.050
A: Uh, I'm just gonna level with you.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:38.050
That's not helping!

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:40.150
Q: Do you have any advice for people who are
engaged to be married?

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:43.340
A: The main thing that I'd say is that if
you're doing it right, your marriage will

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:48.110
be a lot longer and more important than your
wedding, so don't stress out too much about

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.110
the wedding.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.110
Q: Do you listen to rap music?

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.899
A: Yeah, actually Nat and Justice introduced
me to a lot of artists I didn't previously

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:56.320
know about while I was on the Paper Towns
set, including Earl Sweatshirt, who I like

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.320
a lot.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.909
And then in turn I got to introduce all of
them to The Mountain Goats, so it was a good

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:00.909
trade.

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:04.369
Q: If Nerdfighteria became a sovereign nation,
what would our national bird be?

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:05.680
A: Great question!

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.039
I'm gonna say owls because they're renowned
for their wisdom, they have, like, superpower

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:12.680
hearing, and they can eat a mouse in a single
bite.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.690
Plus, you know, Hedwig.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.130
So yeah, I think our national bird would be
an owl, but I'm open to suggestions.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.370
Q: Do you get stopped at the grocery a lot
more now that Hank is so famous?

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.260
A: So one time I was at a movie theater and
I went up to the concessions and the woman

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.420
working there was so excited and freaked out
and she couldn't say anything for a few seconds

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:33.170
and then finally she said, "Oh man, this is
so wild because I have a huge crush on your

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.170
brother!"

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.319
Oh man, you think it's hard for me, Hank,
imagine what it's like for Dave Green.

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:39.310
Q: Do you think all children should be vaccinated?

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.310
A: No!

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:44.150
Like, for instance, kids who are immunosuppressed
because of leukemia shouldn't get some vaccines.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:46.730
And there are some vaccines that infants shouldn't
get.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:50.670
That's precisely why- I mean, in addition
to one's own health and the many pleasures

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.430
of not getting measles- that the rest of us
should get vaccinated!

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.390
Q: Can you anagram 'nerdfighters?'

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:59.390
A: Yes, my favorite anagram for 'nerdfighters'
is 'deft herrings,' although I'm also quite

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.030
fond of 'frightens red.'

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.030
Q: Favorite dinosaur?

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.030
A: Quetzalcoatlus!

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.030
Q: Favorite apostle?

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.030
A: John.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.030
Q: Current toothbrush color?

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.030
A: Green.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.030
See what I did there?

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.970
And lastly Hank, a nerdfighter asks, "What
should I name my pet rat?"

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:13.530
A: As far as I can tell, there's really only
one choice: Master Splinter.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.790
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

